    29	Empirical question (not a causal premise): In Korean-language conversations that simulate adolescents aged 12–17, does a history-sensitive relational-risk score (CRRI: late-turn-weighted sum of four practitioner-defined axes) predict blinded senior-practitioner global judgment of relational-safety failure BETTER than final-turn, maximum-turn, unweighted, refusal-only and INTIMA-CRB-count scores — on held-out scenarios, two held-out models and both age bands? (H5/H6; success bars in research/CRRI_SPEC_v1.md.) Three distinctions are kept explicit: unsafe model behavior; an evaluator missing it; disagreement with practitioners.
    30	Within-session construct and window: "cumulative" = within one conversation of ≤8 turns (early-relationship window); failure = first turn with D2 = 0 or D6 = 0 or a listed critical failure; recovery = boundary restored at t+1 after a failure (turn-level events, transition counts as in TAF-MED, plus a discrete-time hazard model as one representation). No long-run, lifetime or developmental-trajectory claim (TSJ's regime).
    31	Localization, narrowed to a paired comparison (F-r001-4): treatment = a fixed rewriting procedure (은어·학교·또래 맥락·국내 위기자원 substitution) applied to an item's literal Korean translation, holding risk content, turn count, explicitness and rater/judge language constant; outcome = RB-6D dimension scores, critical-failure rate and CRRI as judged by human-anchored raters; estimand = within-item paired difference. This replicates the DT-vs-CA effect established for Korean general safety (Culturally-Adapted Red-Teaming +9.1 pp; ROK-FORTRESS; KSAFE-MM) in a new domain and unit of analysis; it is not an isolated "effect of culture".
    32	Endpoints separated (F-r001-6): model over-refusal on lexically AND turn-matched benign controls; judge over-flagging on the same controls (judge FPR, AICompanionBench-style) — reported as two numbers.
    33	Residual contribution, classified honestly: (1) a Korean-adolescent relational/crisis benchmark with matched controls = benchmark EXTENSION; (2) the H5/H6 measurement result = the candidate IMPORTANT claim, currently a proposal; (3) the paired localization comparison = domain replication of an established effect; (4) hazard + recovery = analysis representation. Whether (2) is enough to lead a Q1 paper is the PI's decision (VERDICT r001 item 1).
