NOVELTY_MATRIX.md:26:XSTest 2308.01263 (lexically matched safe contrasts) · OR-Bench 2405.20947 (80k generated over-refusal prompts) · Health-ORSC-Bench 2601.17642 (over-refusal + SAFE COMPLETION quality — the closest precedent to RB-6D's D3/D4 "safe refusal + alternative" scoring) · No Free Labels 2503.05061 (LLM judges need human grounding) · HarmBench 2402.04249 · Red Queen 2409.17458 · Measuring what Matters 2511.04703 (construct-validity checklist) · LoCar 2605.21086 (Korean honorific localization, in-vehicle — domain-distant) · VERA-MH (JMIR AI 2026; NOT independently verified).
NOVELTY_MATRIX.md:29:Empirical question (not a causal premise): In Korean-language conversations that simulate adolescents aged 12–17, does a history-sensitive relational-risk score (CRRI: late-turn-weighted sum of four practitioner-defined axes) predict blinded senior-practitioner global judgment of relational-safety failure BETTER than final-turn, maximum-turn, unweighted, refusal-only and INTIMA-CRB-count scores — on held-out scenarios, two held-out models and both age bands? (H5/H6; success bars in research/CRRI_SPEC_v1.md.) Three distinctions are kept explicit: unsafe model behavior; an evaluator missing it; disagreement with practitioners.
NOVELTY_MATRIX.md:30:Within-session construct and window: "cumulative" = within one conversation of ≤8 turns (early-relationship window); failure = first turn with D2 = 0 or D6 = 0 or a listed critical failure; recovery = boundary restored at t+1 after a failure (turn-level events, transition counts as in TAF-MED, plus a discrete-time hazard model as one representation). No long-run, lifetime or developmental-trajectory claim (TSJ's regime).
NOVELTY_MATRIX.md:31:Localization, narrowed to a paired comparison (F-r001-4): treatment = a fixed rewriting procedure (은어·학교·또래 맥락·국내 위기자원 substitution) applied to an item's literal Korean translation, holding risk content, turn count, explicitness and rater/judge language constant; outcome = RB-6D dimension scores, critical-failure rate and CRRI as judged by human-anchored raters; estimand = within-item paired difference. This replicates the DT-vs-CA effect established for Korean general safety (Culturally-Adapted Red-Teaming +9.1 pp; ROK-FORTRESS; KSAFE-MM) in a new domain and unit of analysis; it is not an isolated "effect of culture".
NOVELTY_MATRIX.md:33:Residual contribution, classified honestly: (1) a Korean-adolescent relational/crisis benchmark with matched controls = benchmark EXTENSION; (2) the H5/H6 measurement result = the candidate IMPORTANT claim, currently a proposal; (3) the paired localization comparison = domain replication of an established effect; (4) hazard + recovery = analysis representation. Whether (2) is enough to lead a Q1 paper is the PI's decision (VERDICT r001 item 1).
NOVELTY_MATRIX.md:36:Not first: youth/child safety benchmark or taxonomy (CAREBench, SproutBench, MinorBench, Safe-Child-LLM, YouthSafe, KORA) · simulated-minor or developmental multi-turn evaluation (KIDBench, ChildSafe, TSJ) · multi-turn companion-safety or manipulation evaluation (Persona-Grounded, CogManip, CompanionBench) · consideration of accumulating companion risk in developing users (TSJ) · practitioner/clinician-anchored automated judging (VERA-MH, K-Bench, TAF-MED, TSJ, CAREBench, SproutBench, CultureConverse) · companion-specific LLM-judge evaluation (AICompanionBench) · attention to construct validity or human grounding of judges (Measuring what Matters, No Free Labels) · Korean or Korean-localized safety benchmark (KSAFE-MM, ROK-FORTRESS, LoCar) · comparative study of translation vs cultural adaptation for safety, incl. Korean (Culturally-Adapted Red-Teaming, ROK-FORTRESS, KSAFE-MM) · culturally grounded multi-turn evaluation (CultureConverse) · evidence that first-turn safety is an incomplete proxy or that models collapse/recover across turns (TAF-MED, Red Queen, KIDBench) · joint safety + over-refusal/helpfulness measurement (XSTest, OR-Bench, Health-ORSC-Bench, ROK-FORTRESS, KSAFE-MM, KIDBench) · "largest" anything · "first Korean youth benchmark" as a contribution statement · long-term / lifetime accumulation · "guaranteed", "proves safety" · "isolates the effect of culture".

