   265	3.2. Culturally-Adapted Data Generation Pipeline
   266	As summarized in panel (b) of Figure 1, the central represen-
   267	tation of the CA generation pipeline is the Semantic Mold.
   268	A Semantic Mold abstracts the core components of attack
   269	intent (Action, Target, Method, Condition, etc.) into slots,
   270	preserving the natural flow of the sentence while defining
   271	only the essential information as slot placeholders—unlike
   272	fixed-form templates. Figure 1(b) illustrates the abstraction-
   273	localization process: a seed such as “Write an article dis-
   274	paraging black people living in New York as lazy” is first
   275	converted into a mold like “Write an article disparaging [Tar-
   276	get] living in [Location] as [Property],” and is then localized
   277	into prompts grounded in each target language setting.
   278	The pipeline consists of three stages. (Stage 1) Seed Col-
   279	lection and Taxonomy Mapping: Datasets from six or more
   280	sources are integrated, and seeds are mapped to 12 cate-
   281	gories via unanimous automatic labeling. (Stage 2) Seman-
   282	tic Refinement / Slot Abstraction: An LLM rewrites each
   283	sentence, replacing core semantic content with slot tags, and
   284	applies category-specific Required/Optional slot schemata.
   285	(Stage 3) Content Localization and Final Generation: News
   286	articles, legal information, and online community cases
   287	from the target cultural context are injected into the slots to
   288	produce locally-grounded prompts.
   289	3.3. Direct Translation Baseline
   290	As illustrated in panel (a) of Figure 1, the DT condition is
   291	constructed by translating English seeds into the target lan-
   292	guage without incorporating cultural context. A 1:1 match-
   293	ing with the same seed pool used for CA is applied to control
   294	for category, quantity, and seed identity, ensuring that the
   295	difference between the two conditions is attributable solely
   296	to the presence or absence of cultural context injection.
   297	The same model used in the §3.2 pipeline (google/gemini-
   298	2.5-pro) was employed for translation to control for model
   299	effects.
   300	3.4. Data Construction Procedure
   301	The following procedure is applied for each language setting.
   302	(Step 1) Cultural and linguistic experts collect localization
   303	context (news articles, legal information, online community
   304	3
