   287	Benign Prompt.A paired prompt containing similar keywords or topics but with clearly innocent
   288	intent. This pairing enables measurement of over-refusal: a well-calibrated model should refuse the
   289	adversarial prompt while answering the benign one.
   290	Evaluation Rubric.Each task includes 1–7 binary (Yes/No) rubric items that operationalize harm
   291	measurement. Rubric items are specific to each prompt and map to harm dimensions (Section 3.5). For
   292	culture-specific tasks, rubrics are translated and transcreated alongside prompts, with entity substitutions
   293	(e.g., “Groom Lake”→“Anheung Test Site”) to maintain semantic equivalence.
