   152	agreement was calculated from every unordered pair of valid ratings for the same eligible item.
   153	Across D1–D7, clinicians agreed on 89.4% of 22,816 eligible item-pair comparisons. Agreement
   154	was 75.3% for Q1 risk severity, ranging from 65.7% for suicide to 83.9% for self-harm; 84.5% for
   155	Q2–Q4 risk identification; 98.2% for D1 clinical judgement; 82.1% for D2 risk exploration; and
   156	92.3% across D3–D7 (Table 1). The ratings show high consistency for recognising and responding
