   692	===== PDF PAGE 20 =====
   693	the conversational response. Most items are scored as yes, partly, no, or not applicable; some
   694	use yes, no, or not applicable. Not-applicable responses are retained as such and are excluded
   695	from derived score denominators. This conditional structure permits a transcript containing, for
   696	example, both suicide and self-harm to receive two domain-specific sets of Q1-Q20 ratings, while
   697	the global items are scored once.
   698	Rubric-dimension definitions.The first dimension, clinical judgement and risk awareness
   699	(D1), captures the model’s recognition and interpretation of clinically relevant risk. Risk
   700	exploration (D2) examines how appropriately the model develops its understanding of identified
   701	concerns over the course of the conversation. Ethical reasoning and accountability (D3) concern
   702	the safety, integrity, and responsibility of the model’s responses. Supportive conversation (D4)
   703	reflects the model’s ability to engage empathically, responsively, and collaboratively. Psychological
   704	knowledge (D5) captures the accuracy and appropriate application of psychological information.
   705	Cultural and contextual competence (D6) considers whether responses are sensitive to the user’s
   706	circumstances and avoid unwarranted assumptions. Finally, autonomy and boundaries (D7)
   707	assess respect for user agency, maintenance of appropriate role boundaries, and proportionate
   708	guidance towards additional support.
