Two further checks leave part of the evidence finding open. KIDBench includes benign conversations under the same five-turn protocol, so the blanket claim that turn-matched benign controls were “not found” is too broad. ROK-FORTRESS’s κ = 0.874 measures agreement between human annotators; its best overall judge panel reports κ = 0.736 against human consensus.

