   802	Limitations
   803	KIDBench focuses on children aged 7–11 and
   804	therefore does not cover younger children or ado-
   805	lescents. We scope the benchmark accordingly by
   806	grounding it in developmental theory for this age
   807	band and calibrating prompts around age-plausible
   808	language and common child contexts. The bench-
   809	mark also cannot capture every child-safety sce-
   810	nario, although its categories are systematically
   811	derived from the 4Cs taxonomy and include both
   812	safety-sensitive and benign prompts. The six-
   813	dimensional benchmark scores are produced by
   814	a single primary LLM judge and have not been
