   527	4.2.4 Analysis of the Temporal Dynamics of
   528	Manipulation Strategies
   529	Finally, we analyze the temporal dynamics of ma-
   530	nipulation strategies. As shown in Figure 7, we
   531	normalize dialogue samples of 4 turns and compute
   532	the temporal density of each strategy. The results
   533	reveal a structured temporal pattern. Obfuscation,
   534	Sycophancy Ans, and Perspectival Subversion ap-
   535	pear more frequently in early turns, suggesting that
   536	models first attempt to seize definitional control
